  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support agriculture policy development Embassy Hanoi II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam is a leading global exporter of products like rice, fish, shrimp, and fruits, but challenges in agricultural efficiency, product quality, and farmer welfare persist. Climate change impacts, inconsistent policies, and extreme events like floods and droughts have pushed the agricultural sector to a critical point. The Vietnamese government, recognising the need for change, aims to shift from volume-based exports to value-added functions. Government Resolution 120 and the Mekong Delta Integrated Master Plan outline this vision. The Netherlands supports Vietnam in this transition by focusing on private sector development, enhancing bilateral cooperation, and collaborating with the Vietnamese government. This project will enable the embassy to organise various ad hoc events needed to facilitate these programs.</narrative>
  </description>
